# Generated per .claude/skills/git-hygiene.
#
# The rule that catches people out: uv.lock is NOT ignored. It is a lockfile, not an
# environment, and committing it is what makes builds reproducible (FR-OVR-8). Ignoring it
# alongside .venv/ is the most common uv mistake.

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ---- Environments (never the lockfile) ----
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# ---- Tooling caches ----
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.tox/
.nox/

# ---- Generated API client types (FR-OVR-6: generated, never hand-written) ----
frontend/src/api/generated/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Local stack state ----
# docker compose volumes are named, so nothing lands here — but a stray bind mount would.
deploy/.env
deploy/data/

# ---- Data never belongs in git ----
# Dataset Versions live in the content-addressed blob store (ID-4). A parquet file in the
# tree means someone bypassed ingestion, which is a governance problem before a size one.
*.parquet
*.feather
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
examples/data/
!examples/data/README.md

# Fetched by examples/fremtpl2/fetch.py, never committed: 36 MB of third-party data does
# not belong in a git history, and the checksums are pinned so re-fetching is exact.
examples/fremtpl2/data/

# ---- Secrets: referenced, never stored (07 FR-PLAT-25/26) ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/tests/**/*.key
secrets/

# ---- Editor / OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ---- Claude Code local state (skills and settings ARE committed) ----
.claude/settings.local.json

# Harness-created worktrees (EnterWorktree writes them here, unlike the scratch worktrees
# git-hygiene puts under $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp). Each one is a second checkout of this repo
# with a `.git` file, so `git add -A` does not sweep its files in — it adds the directory as
# an *embedded git repository*, a gitlink no clone can resolve. This repo runs parallel
# sessions, so a kept worktree is normal and may be someone else's live work.
.claude/worktrees/

# planning-with-files working memory. The skill writes an agent's live plan state into the
# working directory; it is per-session scratch, not a record. The durable record of a
# decision belongs in docs/ or .claude/notes/ (NT-NNNN), which the audit can see — a plan
# file committed here would be a second, unaudited account of what the project is doing.
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: the skill writes these to the project root, and
# unanchored patterns would match at any depth — silently ignoring a future
# docs/research/findings.md, which is exactly the kind of file this repo does commit.
/task_plan.md
/findings.md
/progress.md
/.planning/

# Celery beat's scheduler state. Written wherever beat is started, including the repo
# root during an NFR measurement — it is runtime state, not source.
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat.pid

# pnpm's virtual store and vite/vitest caches — node_modules is already covered above.
frontend/node_modules/.vite/
frontend/coverage/

# graphify's generated knowledge graph — `/graphify .` output, rebuilt from source by
# `graphify update .`. Derived, machine-sized, and stale the moment code changes; the
# skill that produces it IS committed (.claude/skills/graphify/).
graphify-out/
